# Archive replay roots without a Rules birth read

Source-only question under parent 05d618e2 and ruling 429c1be7.
Neither option below is implemented. Core checkpoint 6a6a7c87 stays unchanged.
The question concerns archive root selection, not live delivery judgment or
private caller-record trust under amendment 608503ab.

## Decision requested

May the room archive keep the existing Rules replay-root selection from a
checked Directory repository row and its finite cohort, treating “rules” as
an expected Native role, then check actual kind if an existing read reaches
that root? This preserves the current no-extra-Rules-read path. The expected
role must never produce CheckedSequence, verified birth, from.pin evidence,
or replayed provenance.

Alternatively, must this selection itself require actual Rules genesis
kind? That requires a separately ruled paid read at this site. The current
path deliberately omits that read. No additional read, new refusal, or
omission of the Rules root is assumed here.

